# House lint configuration.
#
# line_length 120 rather than lintr's 80: matches the rest of the portfolio,
# and the roxygen-heavy extractor files read better unwrapped.
#
# object_name accepts dotted.case alongside snake_case: this package's
# arguments deliberately mirror boostmtree's own naming, which is dotted
# throughout -- `use.rmse` here answers to `cv.flag`, `na.action` and
# `err.rate` there. Renaming them to snake_case would make the plotting layer
# read as though it belonged to a different package than the model it draws.
#
# indentation_linter is off for the same reason it is off in hvtiPlotR: it
# fires on the aligned-argument style used throughout R/ without catching a
# defect.
#
# Everything else is lintr's default and IS enforced. The workflow gates on
# this file, so a genuine false positive belongs behind a `# nolint` carrying
# its reason, not behind a widened rule here.
linters: linters_with_defaults(
    line_length_linter = line_length_linter(120L),
    object_name_linter = object_name_linter(c("snake_case", "dotted.case", "symbols")),
    indentation_linter = NULL
  )
encoding: "UTF-8"
